course: dictionary
lesson: 3375
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Exhaust is one of them. The sentence tells you which meaning you need: «The garage and garden hold a second set of dangers: ... car exhaust with invisible carbon monoxide.» Here exhaust is the gas that comes out of a car, so it is a noun.
explain: Exhaust can also be a verb, a doing word. If a long hike exhausts you, it makes you extremely tired. If you exhaust something, you use it up completely, so nothing is left.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Is there a car, a pipe, or a gas nearby? Then exhaust is the noun. Is someone tired, or is something all used up? Then it is the verb. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Exhaust can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: «Exhaust» as a noun means the waste gas that comes out of a car's engine.
fact: «Exhaust pipe» means the pipe at the back of a car that lets these gases out.
fact: «Exhausted» means extremely tired, and «to exhaust» something means to use it up completely.
fact: Car exhaust fumes harm the air and contain dangerous gases, so never stay near a running engine in a closed garage.
exercise: «Electric cars ... give off no exhaust gases on the road.» What is exhaust in this sentence? | A kind of battery | A road made of stone | *The waste gas that comes out of a car's engine
exercise: «The long hike began to exhaust the children.» What does exhaust mean here? | To wash them in cold water | *To make them extremely tired | To give them a new coat
exercise: Find the word in «Hiding being poor can be exhausting, because one lie usually needs more lies.» Which word means needing a lot of energy and making you very tired? | because | usually | lies | *exhausting
test: «An electric car has no engine burning fuel, so there are no explosions, no exhaust and hardly any noise.» What does exhaust mean here? | *The waste gas from a car | A long, tiring walk | Using up all the petrol
test: Sam says the pipe at the back of the car is the exhaust. Is he right? | Yes, the exhaust pipe lets the gases out | No, the exhaust is the battery under the floor | *Yes, that is exactly what an exhaust pipe is
exam: Jayden reads, «The team tried to exhaust every option before choosing.» What does exhaust mean? | *To use up or try every one | The gas that comes out of a car | To make the team extremely tired | A pipe at the back of a car
